    "created_at": "2022-01-18T18:09:20Z",
    "updated_at": "2022-01-18T18:09:20Z",
    "body": "Yeah, I think the modern version would be to use a namespace (and rename to `TestUtils`, since namespaces are typically uppercased). This avoids the implication that it's an instance of a class, which doesn't really fit.\r\n\r\nThe caveat is that namespaces are kind of minimal right now, with the plan being to add any features to them that we need as we need them. So you might run into gaps in the future.\r\n\r\nThe upside is that the following code works with a namespace:\r\n\r\n```js\r\nconst { gc } = TestUtils;\r\ngc();\r\n```\r\n\r\nbut the corresponding code does not work with an interface (since it'd be missing the `this` object, i.e. it only works if you call it as a method `testUtils.gc()` or `gc.call(testUtils)`).",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
